1. Requirements: 13-item list

Budget — minimum-cost implementation
Terminal types — wired and wireless
Terminal counts — (F1: 10 wired/100 wireless) (F2 & F3: 200 wired/50 wireless each) (reserved floors: 500 wired/200 wireless)
Network management — SNMP, unified
Availability — Layer 3 redundancy and failover
Security — traffic must be controlled
Internet access — static IP at egress
Expansion — no device replacement when new floors come online
Wired VLANs — Servers, GM Office, Admin, Marketing, R&D, per-floor L2 mgmt, reserved interconnect VLANs
Wireless VLANs — separate client VLAN and separate management VLAN per floor
IP/DHCP/gateway — Gateway stays on  aggregate layers while dhcp server handsout ip 
WLAN — single AC managing all APs; F1 registers at L2, F2/F3 at L3; one SSID per floor, WPA-WPA2+PSK+AES, unique password per floor
Security/egress — guest SSID blocked from intranet; only wireless reaches Internet; static public IP; NAT exposes only the web server (port 80)
Management — SNMPv3 with auth+encryption; all devices reachable by NMS; alarms reported

(Numbering kept as a flat list here for traceability back to the README's Met/Next-Steps split, which references these by number.)

